Software and scientific provenance
----------------------------------

This repository extends the coordinate-descent formulation and deep resistive
network simulation framework introduced by:

Benjamin Scellier, "A fast algorithm to simulate nonlinear resistive
networks," Proceedings of the 41st International Conference on Machine
Learning, Proceedings of Machine Learning Research 235:43477-43503, 2024.
https://proceedings.mlr.press/v235/scellier24a.html

The original work treats ideal-diode nonlinear resistive networks. This
artifact builds on that layered DRN model, odd-even coordinate-update scheme,
and equilibrium-propagation training framework while adding the non-ideal
single-Shockley, antiparallel double-Shockley, and measured piecewise-linear
nonlinearities studied in the accompanying paper.

The core model and training subset under repro/vendor is adapted from the
MIT-licensed research code whose original copyright is retained above and in
LICENSE. Subsequent solver, reproduction, documentation, and experiment-runner
changes are copyright (c) 2026 Filip Osana.

